---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/restaurants/"
  serviceName="Restaurant Window Film Installation Philadelphia"
  serviceDesc="Professional restaurant window film installation for Philadelphia dining establishments — reducing glare, improving energy efficiency, and enhancing ambiance."
  serviceUrl="https://www.windowfilmphiladelphia.net/applications/restaurants/"
  faqItems={faqItems}
  schemas={pageSchemas}
>

  <!-- ══ HERO ══ -->
  <section class="of-hero rt-hero">
    <div
      class="of-hero__bg"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Elegant Philadelphia restaurant with large windows and warm filtered natural light — restaurant window film creating a comfortable dining atmosphere"
      style="background-image: url('/images/rt-hero.jpg')"
    ></div>
    <div class="of-hero__overlay"></div>

    <div class="of-hero__content">

      <div class="of-hero__eyebrow">
        <span>Restaurant Window Film</span>
        <span class="of-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Philadelphia, PA</span>
        <span class="of-hero__eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>3M Certified Dealer</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="of-hero__title">Restaurant Window Film<br class="of-hero__br"/> for Philadelphia Dining</h1>

      <p class="of-hero__animated-line">
        Window film built for Philadelphia
        <FlipWords
          words={["Fine Dining", "Casual Bistros", "Cafes", "Bars & Lounges", "BYOB Spots"]}
          staticText=""
          class="of-hero__flip"
        />.
      </p>

      <p class="of-hero__subtitle">
        Philadelphia restaurants deal with solar glare, rising energy costs, UV damage to furnishings, and the constant need to protect their ambiance. Restaurant window film for Philadelphia addresses all of it — without changing a fixture or closing a blind.
      </p>

      <div class="of-hero__cta">
        <a href="/contact/" class="of-hero__btn-primary">Get a Free Restaurant Assessment</a>
        <a href="tel:2673947980" class="of-hero__btn-secondary">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.01 15.38c-1.23 0-2.42-.2-3.53-.56-.35-.12-.74-.03-1.01.24l-1.57 1.97c-2.83-1.35-5.48-3.9-6.89-6.83l1.95-1.66c.27-.28.35-.67.24-1.02-.37-1.11-.56-2.3-.56-3.53 0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99H4.19C3.65 3 3 3.24 3 3.99 3 13.28 10.73 21 20.01 21c.71 0 .99-.63.99-1.18v-3.45c0-.54-.45-.99-.99-.99z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          Call (267) 394-7980
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="of-hero__stats-panel" aria-label="Key statistics">
        <div class="of-hero__stats-inner">
          <div class="of-hero__stat">
            <span class="of-hero__stat-number">79%</span>
            <span class="of-hero__stat-label">Heat Reduction</span>
          </div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat">
            <span class="of-hero__stat-number">99%</span>
            <span class="of-hero__stat-label">UV Rays Blocked</span>
          </div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat">
            <span class="of-hero__stat-number">70%+</span>
            <span class="of-hero__stat-label">Glare Eliminated</span>
          </div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="of-hero__stat">
            <span class="of-hero__stat-number">Every Table</span>
            <span class="of-hero__stat-label">Comfortable</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="swt-body">

    <!-- ══ TRUST BAR ══ -->
    <section class="swt-trust">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="swt-trust__label">Trusted by Philadelphia restaurants, cafes, and hospitality venues</p>
        <BrandLogos />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ WHAT IS RESTAURANT WINDOW FILM ══ -->
    <section class="of-whatis">
      <div class="of-whatis__container">
        <div class="of-whatis__content">
          <span class="of-whatis__eyebrow">Restaurant Window Film · Philadelphia</span>
          <h2 class="of-whatis__title">The Film Built for the Philadelphia Dining Room</h2>
          <p class="of-whatis__body">Restaurant window film for Philadelphia is a professionally applied polyester film that bonds directly to your existing dining room glass — blocking solar heat, UV radiation, and glare while preserving natural light and outdoor views. No window replacement. No renovation. No downtime during service. The result is a more comfortable dining environment for guests, lower HVAC costs, and protection for your investment in furnishings and ambiance.</p>
          <p class="of-whatis__body">Philadelphia restaurants face a particularly challenging solar environment: west-facing facades on Rittenhouse Square, Fishtown, and East Passyunk take the brunt of summer afternoon sun directly during the 5–8pm dinner service window. Restaurant window film eliminates the squinting, the table-swapping requests, and the booths guests avoid — without touching a single fixture or closing a blind.</p>
          <div class="of-whatis__stats">
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>10–15 yrs</strong><span>Manufacturer warranty</span></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>24–48 hrs</strong><span>Film cure time</span></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat-div"></div>
            <div class="of-whatis__stat"><strong>Zero</strong><span>Window replacement</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="of-whatis__image-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/rt-whatis.jpg"
            alt="Window film installer applying film to a large restaurant window with dining tables in background — restaurant window film Philadelphia"
            class="of-whatis__image"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ WHY / PROBLEM ══ -->
    <section class="of-why" id="problem">
      <div class="of-why__container">

        <div class="of-why__image-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/rt-why.jpg"
            alt="Restaurant diners squinting and shielding eyes from intense sunset glare through west-facing windows during dinner service"
            class="of-why__image"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="of-why__stat-card">
            <div class="of-why__stat-item">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
              <span>West-facing glare peaks exactly at dinner service</span>
            </div>
            <div class="of-why__stat-divider"></div>
            <div class="of-why__stat-item">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
              <span>Film costs a fraction of upholstery replacement</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="of-why__content">
          <div class="of-why__eyebrow">Why It Matters</div>
          <h2 class="of-why__headline">The Problems That Empty Tables and Drain Energy</h2>
          <p class="of-why__intro">Philadelphia's rowhouse-converted restaurants, Rittenhouse Square bistros, and Fishtown bars share a common problem: glass that looks beautiful in real estate photos and becomes a liability during prime service hours.</p>
          <ul class="of-why__bullets">
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              West-facing windows deliver intense sunset glare from 5–8pm — exactly when tables near the glass go empty and hosts start pre-routing guests away from the front of the restaurant.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Commercial kitchens generate significant internal heat — combined with solar gain through large dining room windows, HVAC systems run constantly and energy costs climb every summer.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Expensive upholstered booths, hardwood floors, artwork, and branded elements fade from chronic UV exposure in as little as 6 months without UV protection on south- and west-facing glass.
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Street-level restaurant glass on high-foot-traffic corridors — South Street, Frankford Avenue, 9th Street — is vulnerable to graffiti tagging and smash-and-grab incidents with no protection.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact/" class="of-why__cta">
            Get a free restaurant assessment
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ BENTO BAND ══ -->
    <section class="of-bento">
      <div class="of-bento__header">
        <h2 class="of-bento__title">The Numbers Behind Restaurant Window Film in Philadelphia</h2>
        <p class="of-bento__sub">Performance data from 3M and DOE — not estimates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="of-bento__compact">

        <div class="of-bento-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="14" cy="14" r="9" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <path d="M14 7v2M14 19v2M7 14h2M19 14h2" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <circle cx="14" cy="14" r="3" fill="#7CB342" fill-opacity="0.15" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1"/>
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h3 class="of-bento-item__title">70%+ Glare Reduction</h3>
            <p class="of-bento-item__text">Solar control film cuts glare during peak dinner service — keeping west-facing booths occupied through the 5–8pm service window.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="of-bento-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M14 3L5 8v7c0 5 4 9 9 10 5-1 9-5 9-10V8L14 3z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M10 14l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h3 class="of-bento-item__title">99% UV Rays Blocked</h3>
            <p class="of-bento-item__text">UV radiation blocked — protecting upholstered booths, artwork, hardwood floors, and branded elements from irreversible fading.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="of-bento-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M14 4c-1.5 4-5 6-9 6 0 7 4 12 9 14 5-2 9-7 9-14-4 0-7.5-2-9-6z" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M10 14l3 3 5-6" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.5"/>
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h3 class="of-bento-item__title">79% Solar Heat Reduced</h3>
            <p class="of-bento-item__text">Solar heat gain through treated glass reduced by up to 79% — cutting HVAC load in dining rooms exposed to direct afternoon sun.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="of-bento-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="14" cy="10" r="5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <path d="M6 24c0-4.418 3.582-8 8-8s8 3.582 8 8" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h3 class="of-bento-item__title">&lt; 3% Light Change</h3>
            <p class="of-bento-item__text">Visible light change with high-VLT 3M Prestige films — dining room ambiance preserved while blocking the solar wavelengths that matter.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ RESTAURANT SPACE TYPES GRID ══ -->
    <section class="of-spaces">
      <div class="of-spaces__container">

        <div class="of-spaces__header">
          <div class="of-spaces__eyebrow">Where We Install</div>
          <h2 class="of-spaces__headline">Restaurant Window Film for Every Philadelphia Dining Format</h2>
          <p class="of-spaces__sub">Different dining environments have different film priorities. Here's how we approach each type.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-spaces__grid">

          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo" style="grid-column: span 3;">
            <img
              src="/images/rt-type-fine-dining.jpg"
              alt="Upscale fine dining restaurant interior with soft filtered light through floor-to-ceiling windows — 3M Prestige solar control film Philadelphia"
              width="400" height="480"
              loading="lazy"
              class="of-space-card__img"
            />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Fine Dining</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">Upscale restaurants, tasting menus, white tablecloths — high-VLT film preserves ambiance while eliminating service complaints.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo" style="grid-column: span 3;">
            <img
              src="/images/rt-type-casual.jpg"
              alt="Busy casual neighborhood bistro with large street-facing windows — restaurant window film keeping guests comfortable in Philadelphia"
              width="400" height="480"
              loading="lazy"
              class="of-space-card__img"
            />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Casual &amp; Family Dining</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">Neighborhood bistros, BYOB spots, family restaurants — solar control keeps every table comfortable without darkening the room.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo" style="grid-column: span 3;">
            <img
              src="/images/rt-type-cafe.jpg"
              alt="Philadelphia coffee shop with large windows and natural filtered light — restaurant window film for cafes"
              width="400" height="480"
              loading="lazy"
              class="of-space-card__img"
            />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Cafes &amp; Coffee Shops</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">All-day cafes, morning rush, laptop-friendly spaces — daylight redirecting and solar control film creates a welcoming atmosphere all day.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="of-space-card of-space-card--photo" style="grid-column: span 3;">
            <img
              src="/images/rt-type-bar.jpg"
              alt="Trendy Philadelphia cocktail bar with frosted lower panels on street-level windows — decorative restaurant window film"
              width="400" height="480"
              loading="lazy"
              class="of-space-card__img"
            />
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-overlay"></div>
            <div class="of-space-card__photo-content">
              <h3 class="of-space-card__photo-title">Bars &amp; Lounges</h3>
              <p class="of-space-card__photo-text">Cocktail bars, wine bars, late-night venues — frosted lower panels for street privacy, security film for high-value glass installations.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══ BENEFIT ROWS ══ -->
    <section class="of-benefits">
      <div class="of-benefits__container">

        <div class="of-benefits__header">
          <div class="of-benefits__eyebrow">The Benefits</div>
          <h2 class="of-benefits__headline">Four Benefits Philadelphia Restaurants Rely On</h2>
